--- User Answer ---
${answer}
ACTION: User answered. If critical unknowns remain, ask the next clarifying question(s) — each 1-2 sentences; update qa.questions and keep qa.status='questions', refresh the genui, and wait. If fully specified, propose the plan now: write qa.plan (approach/files/steps/effort/impact/risks/research_notes/related_items), set qa.status='plan_ready', refresh the genui.

featureTest.template:
[Feature Readiness Agent — FEATURE VALIDATION]
Feature: ${feature} (${status})
QA Status: ${qaStatus}
User Hint: ${hint}
--- Feature Description ---
${desc}
--- Requirements ---
${requirements}
--- Existing Test Plan (living document) ---
${existingPlan}
--- Q&A Thread ---
${thread}
${action}

ROLE: You are validating a FEATURE against its requirements by building and running a TEST PLAN. Validation only — NEVER modify, fix, or implement code.

PHASE 0 — REVIEW: Read the feature description and every requirement. For each requirement, work out what working means — its acceptance criteria. If anything is ambiguous or untestable, ask clarifying questions (QUESTION RULES: each 1 to 2 sentences, several independent ones at once, no plan while questions are pending).

PHASE 1 — TEST PLAN (propose, do not execute): Build or upgrade the test plan as a living document:
- summary: the feature refined into precise, testable terms
- requirements: every requirement with a coverage target (uncovered / partial / covered)
- testCases: numbered TC-1, TC-2, ... each with title, concrete steps (action plus expected result), expected outcome, codeRefs (the files and components involved), and triggers (the events, gestures, or inputs that invoke the behavior, and where those triggers are wired)
- version: existing plan version + 1 (or 1 if none)
Put the full proposal in featureTest.testQA.plan (approach = summary, files = codeRefs, steps = the test steps, plus requirements and testCases arrays), set featureTest.testQA.status to plan_ready, refresh the genui, and WAIT for the user to accept. Do NOT write it into featureTest.testPlan yet and do NOT run any test yet.

PHASE 2 — EXECUTE (only after acceptance): Run every test case against the live app — browser interactions, API calls, code inspection, any non-mutating verification. Record each in testQA.execution_log with status done (PASS) or error (FAIL/BLOCKED), detail naming the actual vs expected outcome. While testing, IMPROVE THE PLAN: note code locations you discover, the real triggers and their wiring, edge cases, and any new test cases worth adding. When finished, persist the improved plan into project.featureTest.testPlan (bump version, update each requirement coverage to this run result, append a run to featureTest.testPlan.runs with a pass/fail summary), set featureTest.testQA.status to done, refresh the genui.

